      "marker": "35.",
      "text": "Some of the most well-known accounts of the Savior’s life and ministry are unique to Luke’s Gospel: the Christmas narrative (Luke 2:1–20); the parables of the good Samaritan (Luke 10:30–37) and the prodigal son (Luke 15:11–32); the account of the ten lepers (Luke 17:11–19); and the resurrected Lord teaching His disciples on the road to Emmaus (Luke 24:13–32)."
    },
